Audit of Debian GNU/Linux 12 (bookworm): 29 controls

STATUS   ID       SEVERITY  CONTROL
FAIL     SSH-001  medium    Root login disabled
         permitrootlogin is without-password, expected no
         Root is the one account name every scanner tries, and its actions are
         not tied to a person. Log in as a named user and use sudo.
         fix: not automated yet
FAIL     SSH-002  high      Password authentication disabled
         passwordauthentication is yes, expected no
         Passwords can be guessed or reused from leaks; SSH keys cannot be
         brute-forced.
         fix: not automated yet
PASS     SSH-003  high      Keyboard-interactive authentication disabled
PASS     SSH-004  high      Empty passwords rejected
FAIL     SSH-005  low       X11 forwarding disabled
         x11forwarding is yes, expected no
         A server has no use for graphical apps, and a forwarded display lets
         the server reach into your desktop session.
         fix: not automated yet
PASS     SSH-006  low       Host-based authentication disabled
PASS     SSH-007  low       User environment files ignored
FAIL     SSH-008  low       Repeated failed logins are slowed down
         sshd has no PerSourcePenalties (OpenSSH before 9.8) and fail2ban's sshd
         jail is not running
         Bots try common passwords all day. Holding back an address that keeps
         failing cuts the log noise and slows down a guess at a weak password.
         fix: sudo vps-ready apply --module ssh.bruteforce
SKIP     KRN-001  low       Kernel pointers hidden
SKIP     KRN-002  low       Kernel log restricted to root
SKIP     KRN-003  medium    Unprivileged BPF disabled
SKIP     KRN-004  medium    ptrace scope restricted
SKIP     KRN-005  medium    Symlink protection enabled
SKIP     KRN-006  medium    Hardlink protection enabled
SKIP     KRN-007  low       FIFO protection enabled
SKIP     KRN-008  low       Regular file protection enabled
SKIP     KRN-009  low       Setuid core dumps restricted
SKIP     KRN-010  medium    Address space randomization fully enabled
SKIP     KRN-011  low       Kernel profiling restricted
SKIP     NET-001  low       TCP SYN cookies enabled
SKIP     NET-002  low       Source-routed packets rejected
SKIP     NET-003  low       Broadcast pings ignored
SKIP     NET-004  low       IPv4 reverse path filtering enabled
SKIP     NET-005  medium    IPv4 ICMP redirects not accepted
SKIP     NET-006  low       IPv4 ICMP redirects not sent
FAIL     UPD-001  medium    Security updates installed automatically
         unattended-upgrades is not installed;
         APT::Periodic::Update-Package-Lists is not set;
         APT::Periodic::Unattended-Upgrade is not set
         Attackers scan for a flaw soon after its fix is published. Unattended
         upgrades install security fixes on their own, so a server nobody logs
         into still gets them.
         fix: sudo vps-ready apply --module updates.auto
FAIL     FW-001   medium    Incoming traffic denied by default
         no firewall rules filter incoming traffic
         Without it, any service listening on all addresses, such as a database
         left at its defaults, is reachable from the internet. A firewall at
         your provider also protects the server, but this check cannot see it.
         fix: not automated yet
SKIP     FW-002   medium    Container ports do not bypass the firewall
SKIP     MAC-001  medium    AppArmor enabled

4 passed, 6 failed (1 high, 3 medium, 2 low), 0 unknown, 19 skipped
Skipped: kernel settings are not checked inside a container.
Skipped: Docker is not installed.
vps-ready can fix 2 of the 6 (SSH-008, UPD-001): run `sudo vps-ready plan
--module ssh.bruteforce --module updates.auto`.
The other 4 need a manual fix for now; each says so above.
